{#- The brief's layout. Every value arrives escaped from report/brief.py, so nothing here escapes.
    Statements are the summary bullets, finding headings, claim bullets and review bullets, and each
    carries a reference ([C1] or [F1]) that audit.json resolves to the full id. -#}
# Research brief: {{ title }}

Comparison: {{ comparison }}. Run {{ run_id }}, generated {{ generated_at }}, model cost {{ cost }}.

> **Not investment advice.** {{ disclaimer }}

References such as [C1] (a claim) and [F1] (a change) point to `audit.json`, which holds the full
record behind every statement: the claim, its quotes, its metrics and its Tree-of-Thought tree.

## Summary

{% for line in summary %}
- {{ line.text }}{% for ref in line.refs %} [{{ ref }}]{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}

{% for group in groups %}
## {{ group.title }}

{% for finding in group.findings %}
### [{{ finding.ref }}] {{ finding.heading }}

{% if finding.rationale %}
Why it was flagged: {{ finding.rationale }}

{% endif %}
{% for text in finding.texts %}
{{ text.title }}:

{% for line in text.lines %}
> {{ line }}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% if finding.claims %}
{% for claim in finding.claims %}
- **{{ claim.label }}** [{{ claim.ref }}]: {{ claim.text }}
{% for citation in claim.citations %}

{% for line in citation.quote %}
  > {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
  >
  > Source: {{ citation.source }}
{% endfor %}
{% if claim.metrics %}

  Metrics: {{ claim.metrics | join("; ") }}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
{% else %}
No explanation of this change met the evidence standard. See the review section.

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
## Needs review

{% if review %}
{% for item in review %}
- [{{ item.ref }}] {{ item.heading }}: {{ item.reason }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
Nothing in this brief needs review.
{% endif %}
